      "text": [
        " أَخَذَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) حِينَ غَدَا مِنْ مِنًى فِي طَرِيقِ ضَبٍّ وَ رَجَعَ مَا بَيْنَ الْمَأْزِمَيْنِ وَ كَانَ إِذَا سَلَكَ طَرِيقاً لَمْ يَرْجِعْ فِيهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ismail Bin Hammam, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup>, when he<sup>saww</sup> went from Mina, took the Zabb road, and returned by what is between Al-Mazimayn, and it was such that whenever he<sup>saww</sup> travelled by a road, did not return in it (i.e. came back from another way)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Isma‘il ibn Hammam who has said the following: “Abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that the Messenger of Allah, O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause, when leaving Mina moved through the path of Dabb and returned from between al-Mazimin, and when he walked through a path, he would not return by the same path.” "
        ]
      }
    },
